<title>FRANCE: France wants EU to step up free-mkt barley exports.</title>
<headline>France wants EU to step up free-mkt barley exports.</headline>
<byline>Paule Bonjean</byline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>France, which is hoping to export a large part of its bumper barley crop this year, would like the EU to favour free-market supplies over intervention when selling barley on world markets, a top French grain official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>France would like to participate in a large sale of barley to Saudi Arabia but since it has no barley in its intervention stores it can only do so by using free-market supplies.</p>
</text>
